  "scenario": "Connect eqos0 directly to an arm64 macOS peer. Use IPv6 link-local addresses and iperf3 3.22.1 at each end. Request 1000 echoes at a nominal 10 ms interval, one 10-second TCP stream in each direction, then UDP at 300 Mbit/s in each direction. Take EQOS interrupt counters before and after each stream. Repeat with the Plasma service stopped and restore the service. TX and RX are relative to the board.",
  "expected": "Collect bidirectional transfer rates, UDP loss and interrupt rates on the same boot in both service states.",
  "observed": "The gigabit link delivered all 1000 echo replies in each run. In the TCP receive test CPU0 spent 100% of one sample in interrupts with Plasma locked and 99.5% with Plasma stopped. The board restored the desktop after the measurements. DRM and DE reported zero errors.",
